    {
      "id": 59590,
      "name": "Reckless",
      "username": "Reckless",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-12T20:17:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>G-Unity seems to be filled with thematic goodies rather than outright mechanical dominance.&nbsp; Blowing up an Electro-Pulse Explosive or one of Voss's ships is cool thematically rather than a consistent mechanical benefit.&nbsp; Unity blowing up villain Devices is something fans speculated about for a month or two when she was revealed in the Kickstarter.&nbsp; If it doesn't sound terribly fun to you, then I recommend playing her exclusively against villains with Devices or doing your best to keep her alive (which is a game in and of itself).<br><br>I'd rather have a specialized, thematically interesting incapacitated power than an innate power that just zaps 4-18 HP targets for free.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:35:25.951Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
